  "_entry": "Typing an amount, which is a different problem from parsing one. Digits fill up from the CENTS (450 is $4.50) because most amounts in a ledger have cents; a typed '.' overrides that and the string reads the ordinary way, so '50.' is $50.00. The '.00' toggle flips the default for bare digits and a typed dot still wins. A third decimal place is KEPT in the field and reads as null, so a pasted 1.005 is refused rather than quietly becoming 1.00 — the same refusal parseAmount makes, for the same reason. Rows are [what was typed, what the field keeps, cents or null]. Produced by a second implementation written from the prose above rather than from the code.",
